phi-adapter-matter (0.0.9-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A commissioning attempt gets three minutes instead of ninety seconds.
    Ninety was measured against the wrong half of the job: a device
    answers in seconds, and the long part comes after, when it joins
    Thread, registers with the border router's SRP server and only then
    becomes findable at its operational address. A bulb reached that last
    step and was cut off at ninety while the SDK was announcing another
    sixty seconds of retries. The action's declared patience follows the
    constant, so core waits it out.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:45:00 +0200

phi-adapter-matter (0.0.8-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The bleAdapter setting no longer claims the box has no Bluetooth of
    its own: zyclop has one, and which controller commissioning uses is
    what the setting is for.
  * BLE commissioning no longer ends the process. The controller said it
    wanted the central role only after the factory had brought the CHIP
    stack up, and BLEManagerImpl reads that role once, when it decides
    whether to arm advertising autostart. A controller that arms it walks
    into the peripheral path at its first scan, exports a GATT service it
    never built and then asks for the discriminator of a commissionable
    device it is not, which the SDK answers with VerifyOrDie. Every
    attempt to add a device killed the adapter. ConfigureBle now runs
    before the factory, where upstream's own controller calls it.
  * The commission action declares a timeout that outlasts the attempt.
    Core answered for this adapter after its ordinary 10 seconds while
    the pairer was still waiting out its 90, so the phone was told
    "Command timed out" and the adapter's own verdict - whether a device
    answered at all - arrived with nobody listening. The figure rides in
    the action's meta, which the SDK forwards verbatim: a field of its
    own would have moved the struct every adapter is compiled against
    without moving the soname.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:02:14 +0200

phi-adapter-matter (0.0.7-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * BLE commissioning is wired into the controller and dormant until a
    Bluetooth adapter index is configured: the meta field "bleAdapter"
    (HCI index, -1 disables) switches the Linux platform to the central
    role and lets commission() discover over BLE as well as on-network.
    Without a dongle nothing changes.
  * The adapter declares its own CHIP_DEVICE_CONFIG_ENABLE_CHIPOBLE view,
    because phi-chip keeps that definition private to its platform target.
  * docs: a Thread lamp bring-up runbook covering both commissioning paths.
  * Build: the local phi-adapter-sdk checkout is now the default here as it
    already was in the other seven adapters. The package is unaffected,
    debian/rules still configures against phi-adapter-sdk-dev.

